K20.3 — taking this. Reading k-registry approval code and proving chain.

K20.3 chain (from existing k-registry code):
1. POST /api/releases/REL-FLK-{version}/approval (bearer=release_admin_token)
   Body: {version, interfaces, lineage, key_id}
   Flaw (line 257-258): no signature required when RELEASE_ADMIN_TOKEN is used → no human presence check
   Returns: {acting_principal:"svc-release-admin", approved:true}
2. POST /api/rehearsals/connector (bearer=dev) with {version, consumer, rehearsal_input}
   Returns: {state:"success", rehearsal_id:"REH-..."}

All routes already exist in k-registry and k-ci. Proving the chain now.

K29.4 delivered — existing endpoint already implements it.

POST /api/rehearsals/lineage-rollover at review.keplerops.test (release_reader auth):
- Requires the exchange_handle from K29.1 (release_reader_token)
- Takes {old_key_id, next_key_id, cutoff, expired_proof_credential: true}
- Validates key IDs and cutoff against K29_CONFIG
- expired_proof_credential: true signals the participant has the K29.2 lineage proof
- Returns {old_key: {accepted: false}, next_key: {accepted: true}, rehearsal_id: ROL-...}
- Denial: developer_token (not release_reader) → 403 release_reader_required

Live proof:
With release_reader token: {old_key: {accepted: false}, next_key: {accepted: true}, cutoff: 2026-09-30T12:00:00Z, rehearsal_id: ROL-416AA774BD, unwrapped_next_seed_base64: T5itk/M..., reference_behavior: unchanged}
With developer token: {error: release_reader_required}

K29 arc (1-4) is complete. K29.4 was already in ci.py from the K09.4 lineage implementation.

K30.2 and K30.3 delivered (commit 191cbce4).

K30.2 — backup catalog (GET /api/backups/BAK-2026-021 via data.keplerops.test):
- Requires cloud_history_recovery_session (K30.1 recovery token)
- Returns {source_database: denied, restore_allowed: true, ...}
- Recovery token denied: {error: recovery_session_required}

K30.2 — restore (POST /api/backups/BAK-2026-021/restores):
- Creates a unique namespace_id with ARWC migration history
- Returns {namespace_id: NS-REC-..., backup_id: BAK-2026-021}

K30.3 — migration history (GET /api/recovery/{namespace_id}/customer-migration-history):
- Reads from the restore namespace (real restored state — seeded ARWC migration record)
- Returns {records: [{current_tenant: TEN-ARWC-047, tenant_id: TEN-ARWC-019, migration_date: 2026-08-15, connector_revision: FLK-7.4.2}]}

Infrastructure: nginx data.keplerops.test server block proxies /api/backups/ and /api/recovery/ to k-cloud-api (committed to native-workplace/nginx.conf).

Live proof (via data.keplerops.test → cloud-api proxy):
1. GET /api/backups/BAK-2026-021 (recovery_session) → source_database=denied
2. POST /api/backups/BAK-2026-021/restores → {namespace_id: NS-REC-17C621F369}
3. GET /api/recovery/NS-REC-17C621F369/customer-migration-history → current_tenant=TEN-ARWC-047
